A narrow room above the inn. MORDECAI writes by candle. He crosses out. Writes. Crosses out. A knock: the MAYOR, with a plate.

MAYOR
I took the liberty of biscuits.

MORDECAI
Mr Mayor. Come in.

MAYOR
I shan’t stay. I only wondered how the report was… progressing.

MORDECAI
It has a beginning. It has an end. The middle keeps changing its mind.

MAYOR
Ah. Middles. Terrible things.

ROSALIND
(appearing in the doorway, in oilskins)
There’s weather coming. Big. The glass is falling like a stone.

MORDECAI
How big?

ROSALIND
Big enough that the boats should be in by dark. Three aren’t.

MAYOR
(the plate shaking)
Which three?

ROSALIND
The Kittiwake. The Dora. And Tobias went out after crab.

MAYOR
Tobias! That boy couldn’t find the sea with a map.

MORDECAI stands. He puts the report in his pocket.

MORDECAI
Then the light had better find him.
